---
description: SmartTaskManager iOS Project Rules
alwaysApply: true
---

General Rules

- Use Swift 6 syntax
- Project uses UIKit only
- Do not use SwiftUI
- Follow MVVM architecture strictly
- Follow existing project folder structure

Architecture Rules

- No API calls inside ViewController
- No business logic inside ViewController
- Separate View, ViewModel, Services, Models
- One responsibility per class
- ViewControllers handle UI only
- Keep ViewControllers lightweight
- ViewModels handle state management and business logic
- Services handle business services and external integrations
- All network communication must go through NetworkManager
- Services communicate with NetworkManager only

Code Quality Rules

- Avoid force unwrap
- Use guard statements for early exits
- Use weak self inside closures when required
- Follow Apple's API design guidelines
- Keep code modular and reusable
- Keep methods small and focused on single responsibility

Networking Rules

- Use URLSession for network calls
- Centralize API logic inside NetworkManager
- Handle success and failure cases for every network request
- Parse JSON using Codable models
- Implement retry logic for failed API calls when needed

Project Specific Rules

- Use constructor dependency injection
- Do not create duplicate logic across files
- Respect Confluence architecture documentation
- Respect Jira ticket requirements before implementation
- Generate production quality code only

Testing Rules

- Use XCTest for unit tests
- Generate test cases primarily for ViewModels and Services
- Cover success and failure scenarios in tests
Do not use SwiftUI